  <name>Kadence</name>
  <summary>Record, arrange and mix music</summary>
  <description>
    <p>
      Kadence is a digital audio workstation for KDE Plasma. It records and
      plays back multitrack audio and MIDI, hosts CLAP, LV2 and VST3 plugins,
      and talks to PipeWire or JACK.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Record audio and MIDI with a count-in and a metronome</li>
      <li>Arrange clips with fades, clip gain, loops and automation</li>
      <li>Edit notes in the piano roll, with quantize and humanize</li>
      <li>Mix with built-in effects, plugins, sends and buses</li>
      <li>Export the song to WAV or FLAC</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Every plugin runs in a process of its own, so a plugin that crashes
      doesn't take the song with it.
    </p>
  </description>
